id:                     E6412
trigger_tool:           tar|ssh|device-W3|wrapper
phase:                  transfer|preflight|target-validation
error_signature:        archive transfer RC0 but production wrapper reports missing <task-root>/<bundle>/<entrypoint>

severity:               2
category:               transfer, packaging, evidence, transaction
match_keywords:         top-level archive directory, arcname, bundle prefix, extraction namespace, exact-byte transfer, wrapper path contract, tar member list, fresh target root
title:                  Bind transfer archive top-level layout to the production wrapper namespace

root_cause:             Archive byte identity and successful extraction do not prove that the extracted namespace matches the paths resolved by the production controller. Archiving the contents of a named bundle directory removes its top-level component, so the target receives <task-root>/archives and <task-root>/candidate-manifest.tsv while the wrapper requires <task-root>/bundle/archives and <task-root>/bundle/candidate-manifest.tsv. A strict wrapper must reject this before preparation or launch.
affected_scope:         Any target transaction that extracts a frozen archive beneath a task root and resolves inputs below a named directory such as bundle, input, or payload.
verification_cmd:       Inspect archive member names before transfer; require the named root and root-relative members; perform two remote byte-count/SHA-256 readbacks; after extraction read back exact entrypoint, manifest, and cache paths below the expected root; run the wrapper preflight before any prepare or launch.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:            explicit-top-level-archive-and-postextract-namespace-check
rec_description:        Treat the archive root name as a frozen contract field. Add the unique directory with an explicit archive name, compare all members against that prefix, and make the production wrapper validate the same canonical paths. If a wrong-layout transfer has already produced a task root, preserve its receipts, prove the result/execution roots and foreign processes are absent, clean only the task-owned root, and create a successor rather than repairing the consumed run in place.
rec_command:            python tarfile.add(bundle, arcname="bundle"); inspect names; transfer; read back bundle/w3-transaction.sh and bundle/candidate-manifest.tsv; wrapper preflight
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               frozen-transfer-builder-and-production-preflight

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      diagnostic-only-layout-inspection
fallback_description:   A target find listing or local tar table can diagnose a namespace mismatch but cannot replace exact-byte transfer, wrapper preflight, or the complete W3 transaction.
fallback_command:       list the exact task root and expected named child; do not launch or classify the run as PASS
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          read-only-reconciliation

forbid_1_pattern:       tar.*-C.*bundle.*[.]|archive.*contents.*without.*root
forbid_1_reason:        Archiving directory contents without an explicit root drops the namespace required by the controller.
forbid_1_consequence:   Transfer and extraction can report RC0 while the wrapper cannot find its frozen entrypoint and the transaction cannot start.
forbid_2_pattern:       transfer.*SHA.*PASS.*without.*path|extract.*RC0.*W3.*PASS
forbid_2_reason:        Byte and extraction status are necessary but do not prove semantic path binding.
forbid_2_consequence:   A stale or misplaced payload can be interpreted as the current transaction or cause an opaque prelaunch failure.
forbid_3_pattern:       repair.*in-place.*wrong-layout|retransfer.*same.*run_id
forbid_3_reason:        A transfer that created partial remote state is a consumed side-effect boundary even when launch_count remains zero.
forbid_3_consequence:   Rewriting the same run obscures the original failure and risks mixing immutable receipts with a different payload layout.

principles:             P005,P010,P013
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

